## Database Entities
KiloPay Ltd database is made up of the underlisted principal entites:

1.  CUSTOMER
2.  BANK
3.  ACCOUNT
4.  BENEFICIARY
5.  FINANCIAL_TRANSACTION
6.  USER_ACCOUNTSACTION
7.  AUDIT_LOG

### CUSTOMER
Stores information about KiloPay customers. Key attributes include:

customer_id – Primary Key
first_name
last_name
email
phone
date_of_birth
address
registration_date
status

### BANK
Stores information about banks associated with customer accounts and beneficiaries. Key attributes include:

bank_id – Primary Key
bank_name
bank_code

### ACCOUNT
Stores customer bank account information. Key attributes include:

account_id – Primary Key
customer_id – Foreign Key
bank_id – Foreign Key
account_number
account_type
balance
currency
status
date_opened

### BENEFICIARY
Stores information about customer beneficiaries. Key attributes include:

beneficiary_id – Primary Key
customer_id – Foreign Key
bank_id – Foreign Key
beneficiary_name
account_number
nickname
date_added
status

### FINANCIAL_TRANSACTION
Stores financial transactions performed against customer accounts. Key attributes include:

transaction_id – Primary Key
account_id – Foreign Key
transaction_type
amount
transaction_reference
transaction_date
description
status

### USER_ACCOUNT
Stores information about authorized system users. Key attributes include:

user_id – Primary Key
username
full_name
role
email
status
created_at

### AUDIT_LOG
Stores system audit activities for accountability and traceability. Key attributes include:

audit_id – Primary Key
user_id – Foreign Key
action
table_name
record_id
action_timestamp
description

## Entity Relationship
The entities relationship is represented in the Entity Relationship Diagram (ERD) included is this portfolio. See ERD.png. The relationship is summarise bewlo:

1.  A CUSTOMER can have one or more ACCOUNTS.
2.  A BANK can be associated with multiple ACCOUNTS.
3.  A CUSTOMER can have multiple BENEFICIARIES.
4.  A BANK can be associated with multiple BENEFICIARIES.
5.  An ACCOUNT can have multiple FINANCIAL_TRANSACTIONS.
6.  A USER_ACCOUNT can generate multiple AUDIT_LOG records.
7.  Each AUDIT_LOG record is associated with one system user.

## Database Design
Relational database model principle is adopted for the database design.

### Primary Keys
Each major entity has a unique primary key used to identify individual records.

CUSTOMER: customer_id
BANK: bank_id
ACCOUNT: account_id
BENEFICIARY: beneficiary_id
FINANCIAL_TRANSACTION: transaction_id
USER_ACCOUNT: user_id
AUDIT_LOG: audit_id

### Foreign Keys
Foreign keys are used to establish relationships between entities and maintain referential integrity. Such as

ACCOUNT.customer_id to CUSTOMER.customer_id
ACCOUNT.bank_id  to BANK.bank_id
BENEFICIARY.customer_id to CUSTOMER.customer_id
BENEFICIARY.bank_id to BANK.bank_id
FINANCIAL_TRANSACTION.account_id to ACCOUNT.account_id
AUDIT_LOG.user_id to USER_ACCOUNT.user_id

